# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .dockerignore
#
# The critical entry is node_modules: your host tree contains a half-built
# node-sass compiled against Node 23's ABI. Copying it into a Node 6 image
# would poison the install layer. Dependencies are installed IN the image.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

node_modules
**/node_modules
bower_components
**/bower_components

# NOTE: build/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It is committed in this repo
# (marmelab ship built files), and `make build` does `rm -rf build/*` and
# regenerates it anyway. Ignoring it risks breaking the demo page, which
# references build/ng-admin.min.js.

# NOTE: do NOT add any of these — the build depends on them:
#   Makefile           entire workflow (install / run / build / test)
#   _postinstall.js    invoked by `make install` after npm install
#   webpack.config.js  the build itself
#   examples/          `make run` serves examples/blog as content-base
#   scripts/           check-only-in-tests.sh, called by `make test`
#   npm-shrinkwrap.json  the lockfile npm 3 actually respects

.git
.gitignore
.github
.tmp
.sass-cache
.cache
npm-debug.log*
.npm
.nyc_output
coverage

Dockerfile
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
DOCKER.md

.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
.netrc
.npmrc

.idea
.vscode
*.swp
.DS_Store
